  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 313 AM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nRidging across the western CONUS, will begin to migrate east \nbeginning Thursday with the forecast area not seeing the main \neffects of this airmass until Friday. For Thursday, highs will \nbe in the mid 80s to around 90 in the west. Much warmer \ntemperatures will arrive on Friday across the area with Saturday\nthrough Monday featuring hot temperatures across all of the \nforecast area. The latest NBM continues to trend higher with its\nforecast temps Friday through Monday and is reflected with this\nforecast package. Looking at the GFS ensembles and their mean \nhighs, North Platte could see 100+ degree readings Friday \nthrough Monday. The deterministic GFS soln has H85 temps of 30+ \nC across SW Nebraska with some locations in far SW Nebraska \neclipsing 35C Friday through Monday. With temperatures trending \nupward in the NBM and with support from the deterministic and \nensemble GFS solns, will probably begin to message the heat for \nthe end of the week. As for precipitation chances, they appear \nlimited through Monday. However, by Monday, a northern stream \ntrough may force a frontal boundary into northern Nebraska which\nmay lead to increased chances for showers and thunderstorms \nover northern Nebraska. Forecast confidence is low ATTM and pops\nwere not increased over the slight chance, low end chance pops \nwith the inherited forecast.",
